"{\n  \"reasoning\": \"Using high gm/Id (24) for input NMOS reduces tail current to meet power budget. L=2\u202f\u00b5m gives high output resistance for gain. PMOS load uses gm/Id=8 and L=2\u202f\u00b5m to keep gm low, moving the pole below GBW for >60\u00b0 PM. Tail NMOS uses gm/Id=12, L=0.5\u202f\u00b5m for adequate Vdsat. Calculated Itail\u224813\u202f\u00b5A gives GBW\u22485\u202fMHz, A0\u224851\u202fdB, PM\u224862\u00b0, power\u224886\u202f\u00b5W, swing >1.5\u202fV, all widths within 0.22\u20112000\u202f\u00b5m.\",\n  \"gmid1\": 24,\n  \"L1_um\": 2.0,\n  \"gmid3\": 8,\n  \"L3_um\": 2.0,\n  \"gmid5\": 12,\n  \"L5_um\": 0.5,\n  \"Itail_uA\": 13\n}"